-id "q-97631" :question/problem "A particle moves along a circular path centered at $O$ in the $xy$-plane in the counterclockwise direction with a constant angular velocity of $1\\text{ rad/s}.$ Given that the object is at the position $(4,0)$ when $t=0,$ find the position function of the particle." :question/worked-solution "The position function of a particle moving in a circular path of radius $R$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity $\\omega $ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t\\,j),\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that the circle is centered at $O,$ and the particle is at the position $(R,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nSince the object's initial position is $(4,0),$ we have that $r(0)=4i,$ and we can conclude that the circle's radius is $R=4.$\n\nTherefore, since we have $R=4$ and $\\omega =1\\text{ rad/s},$ we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-97631/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb1745c5-6485-5a9d-9e8f-19492928e4b4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97631"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97638/selection/cc34ea2c116b08d4bf59ebf62adfea473033410720748604f29a551b878e4fe2" :answer/id #uuid "f2be6c5c-760d-5f0b-8284-2f73880b551c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(t)=\\pi (\\operatorname{cos}⁡6t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡6t\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97638/selection/b11e5b908d0468cd8d87da22613216ef750ffe76bb33ff96429b3d1299cb9d72" :answer/id #uuid "7bec854f-de12-5953-b47c-d6f5b420639a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(t)=-6(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97638/selection/edcab843e9df0f5628f2e44ab3332e6f4d6abd091631d7c5449b3dd4ea3e7d14" :answer