a circular path of radius $R$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity $\\omega $ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t\\,i+a\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t\\,j),\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that the circle is centered at $O,$ and particle is at the position $(R,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nSince the object's initial position is $(6,0),$ we have that $r(0)=\\,6i,$ and we can conclude that the radius of the circle $R=6.$\n\nTherefore, since we have $R=6$ and $\\omega =-\\pi \\text{ rad/s}$ (negative because the motion is clockwise), we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =6(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi t)\\,j) \\\\  & =6(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\,j).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97638/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb1745c5-6485-5a9d-9e8f-19492928e4b4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97638"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97633/selection/8089ed6a0f9a6109867ec569f1da29b2b946ed22bbc17c547fb547a52c552a99" :answer/id #uuid "c13535d1-8134-5e24-853e-b6788cec800d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(t)=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97633/selection/89ebae41e729b20ff3fdeeb652f3a14be6b319270635f2b9ba0126b78e30542c" :answer/id #uuid "afc75da7-f7be-5cad-a005-67e0e8019b6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(t)=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97633/selection/f34628f91f4cb141040f9757921f35b291c4a3a383fac4cb32e7e620831a1b7d" :answer/id #uuid "4a3b2b71-cb1b-5a37-a61a-625120986dee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(t)=3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{t}{2}\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{t}{2}\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9763