torname{sin}⁡\\omega t\\,j),\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that the circle is centered at $O,$ and the particle is at the position $(R,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nSince the object's initial position is $(3,0),$ we have that $r(0)=3i,$ and we can conclude that the circle's radius is $R=3.$\n\nTherefore, since we have $R=3$ and $\\omega =\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ rad/s},$ we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{t}{2}\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{t}{2}\\,j).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-97633/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb1745c5-6485-5a9d-9e8f-19492928e4b4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97633"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97632/selection/6b31c927e18efe65f80cb115713138e03c688c3e9dbc34de38f40acdfa144bb2" :answer/id #uuid "3310cee0-0b73-5481-b5a8-33d661cf8481" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(t)=4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡8t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡8t\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97632/selection/ccdd17460bb7d05e5293e891675a2213e2dc51613855b79227f34b12de49ac5c" :answer/id #uuid "da77c241-2a0f-5895-9a63-22797e533003" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(t)=8(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97632/selection/90753abb33d6cbd22cd3576b06333ed604c6c644a65c1bb0456d528edfccc950" :answer/id #uuid "56a78a97-58eb-5051-9db5-ff2eedf13a17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(t)=4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡8t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡8t\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97632/selection/fffca9ec8dbd3b132cc06e5cc9a73f0b616d975d67f0a0e0c937750f0065fbb0" :answer/id #uuid "ff9c3807-399d-5ff2-ad2b-08a91e302202" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(t)=8(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97632/selection/f9100d31