e position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =8(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\,j).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-97632/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb1745c5-6485-5a9d-9e8f-19492928e4b4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97632"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97639/selection/8d5fd544bd3e578c00390e7c8f8335b40a4682c3eab40b8e0f96ff63a8e70725" :answer/id #uuid "5dc585d8-1f02-5831-a505-a5294826095d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36\\text{ m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97639/selection/9b82054e069ad052ea81b72efe81172644f90ad4382dc8c17056e6ba37883b7b" :answer/id #uuid "b4c4c627-db0f-57ad-bcc8-9d7d629565b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\text{ m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97639/selection/efb4f776698e70ba708659fa4660be754f72cba555654d50b3060e615202e50a" :answer/id #uuid "52eeaa54-b7ea-56f1-b9e8-d89c723f3713" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\text{ m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97639/selection/66de307a29dbf354c72ac492f1b341569fe39c4edfd038402f7f6533aa06deee" :answer/id #uuid "538115b1-0f85-564b-b857-ebbf2d0d44f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\text{ m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97639/selection/7afee980936b18fb28c69baee715dadd30b749e8a447bbeae89d7e3f3b2c7636" :answer/id #uuid "418b4b19-b67e-5e2d-bd1b-a065d9959d39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\text{ m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97639/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7de086bf-c5d8-5c17-8302-5871bfb2fc55" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97639/selection/efb4f776698e70ba708659fa4660be754f72cba555654d50b3060e615202e50a" :answer-field/choices ["q-97639/selection/8d5fd544bd3e578c00390e7c8f8335b40a4682c3eab40b8e0f96ff63a8e70725" "q-97639/selection/9b82054e069ad052ea81b72efe81172644f90ad4382dc8c17056e6ba37883b7b" "q-97639/selection/efb4f776698e70ba708659fa4660be754f72cba555654d50b3060e615202e50a" "q-97639/selection/66de307a29dbf354c72ac492f1b341569fe39c4edfd038402f7f6533aa06deee" "q-97639/selection/7afee980936b18fb28c69baee715dadd30b749e8a447bbeae89d7e3f3b2c7636"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97639" :question/id #uuid "edacd334-f108-5749-a895-3b5b85eb889e" :question/math-academy-id "q-97639" :question/problem "An object moves along a circular path with position $r(t)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ meters. Find the speed of the object at time $t,$ measured in seconds." :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we find the velocity vector by differentiating the position vector. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =(r(t))^{′} \\\\  & =(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j)^{′} \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed, we calculate the magnitude of the velocity vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}||v(t)|| & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+16{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed of the object is $4\\text{ m/s}.$\n\nNote that the speed is constant, but the velocity is not. \n\n**Method 2**\n\nFor uniform circular motion in the $xy$-plane, we have\n\n$$\n||v||=R|\\omega |,\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the radius of the circle, and $\\omega $ is the angular velocity.\n\nIn our case, the radius of the circle is $R=4\\,\\text{m}$ and the angular frequency $\\omega =1\\,\\text{rad/s}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n||v||=4\\cdot |1|=4\\text{ m/s}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-97639/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "77d9865d-2e8e-59fe-9a81-8935df037303"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97639"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97663/selection/27663c651b11427cb99cd87a1cc5f4f02ecb57d9c129a80f4aba5376ffc5fb45" :answer/id #uuid "9388ac87-4c11-568b-ad76-4d785967e944" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\,i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97663/selection/4e305c1888f099cb36109dbb8fcc76e1d66969612bc9f0f8df823dd929b9a7d6" :answer/id #uuid "5c24196b-047c-5cc4-b2ac-e5ebd18462c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\,i-8\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97663/selection/9f3b38e668703c9fac654438c3618214b2b694640d2b458a0ffb49128cd692ac" :answer/id #uuid "ba221c4c-bca3-5bd4-93be-7e9f8eefe93d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-24\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97663/selection/f0ad3cad9c01d21a1c6d622b464ed87bfa025063528546472b668566e6ea5ca7" :answer/id #uuid "7e228115-1486-5642-a04b-52ef7e41a363" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97663/selection/d91edb52b0ad8752a2cf192333d35d2c4295c5a296994fd662a401eef0ebd284" :answer/id #uuid "0b3c314e-f55a-53f9-a470-a9cb42e8c20b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12\\,i+12\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97663/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c38bf45-dd66-55e0-90b1-ea3c3d6ad229" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97663/selection/9f3b38e668703c9fac654438c3618214b2b694640d2b458a0ffb49128cd692ac" :answer-field/choices ["q-97663/selection/27663c651b11427cb99cd87a1cc5f4f02ecb57d9c129a80f4aba5376ffc5fb45" "q-97663/selection/4e305c1888f099cb36109dbb8fcc76e1d66969612bc9f0f8df823dd929b9a7d6" "q-97663/selection/9f3b38e668703c9fac654438c3618214b2b694640d2b458a0ffb49128cd692ac" "q-97663/selection/f0ad3cad9c01d21a1c6d622b464ed87bfa025063528546472b668566e6ea5ca7" "q-97663/selection/d91edb52b0ad8752a2cf192333d35d2c4295c5a296994fd662a401eef0ebd284"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97663" :question/id #uuid "eab4ecdb-5a78-5f89-80df-0b7c97be20cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-97663" :question/problem "A particle $P$ moves along a counterclockwise circular path centered at $O$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity of $8\\,\\text{rad/s}.$ Given that the particle is located at $(3,0)$ when $t=0,$ find the velocity of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "The position function of a particle moving in a circular path of radius $R$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity $\\omega $ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t\\,j),\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that the circle is centered at $O,$ and the particle is at the position $(R,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nIn our case, we have $R=3$ and $\\omega =8\\text{ rad/s},$ so we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡8t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡8t\\,j).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the velocity vector by differentiating the position vector. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =(3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡8t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡8t\\,j))^{′} \\\\  & =-24\\operatorname{sin}⁡8t\\,i+24\\operatorname{cos}⁡8t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the velocity vector at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{8},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =-24\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8})\\,i+24\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8})\\,j \\\\  & =-24\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi \\,i+24\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi \\,j \\\\  & =-24\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97663/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "77d9865d-2e8e-59fe-9a81-8935df037303"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97663"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-97541"] :question/problem "An object moves along a circular path with position $r(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\,j$ meters. Find the speed of the object at time $t,$ measured in seconds." :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we find the velocity vector by differentiating the position vector. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =(r(t))^{′} \\\\  & =(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\,j)^{′} \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\,i+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed, we calculate the magnitude of the velocity vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}||v(t)|| & =\\sqrt{(-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)^{2}+(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36{sin}^{2}⁡3t+36{cos}^{2}⁡3t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36({sin}^{2}⁡3t+{cos}^{2}⁡3t)} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed of the object is $6\\text{ m/s}.$\n\nNote that the speed is constant, but the velocity is not. \n\n**Method 2**\n\nFor uniform circular motion in the $xy$-plane, we have\n\n$$\n||v||=R|\\omega |,\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the radius of the circle, and $\\omega $ is the angular velocity.\n\nIn our case, the radius of the circle is $R=2\\,\\text{m}$ and the angular frequency $\\omega =3\\,\\text{rad/s}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n||v||=2\\cdot |3|=6\\text{ m/s}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-97665/selection/f2e36a58802362203d214917413eacbec44cc25e6ecd3c5d7c4679d9f9d493fd" :answer/id #uuid "82c8c7c6-e94a-5b0b-96b0-ebe8c7e5fbe6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\,i-7\\sqrt{3}j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97665/selection/ce8c2bcaef40d99863207e29506d40a17a312537ce24a742c9ed3d1ae307e6bf" :answer/id #uuid "9c183267-1dc9-594d-a988-f75b0c8f085e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7\\sqrt{3}\\,i+7j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97665/selection/495e8813f59ee3e6319824a6a3a2161fda3a98a295c7e365f9389d8c70b6c8d4" :answer/id #uuid "a4776b89-312d-5184-9040-869cab14cfa4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97665/selection/ec7ad9636cc54d887852e0674981ad4b02d15305f909ec6668bfa91951089a50" :answer/id #uuid "54564807-687a-5a8f-bc77-fd4bcdea3c13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7\\sqrt{3}\\,i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97665/selection/beb61f7e98d5c8f83c610d16a577a27e9b26dd4a8e94eef9a7c5efedbe64b015" :answer/id #uuid "7f4d415e-38b8-5d2d-8673-bbaf152e1ea3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-14\\sqrt{3}\\,i+14j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97665/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "009b9535-b7f3-502d-bf60-cc456a35816e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97665/selection/ce8c2bcaef40d99863207e29506d40a17a312537ce24a742c9ed3d1ae307e6bf" :answer-field/choices ["q-97665/selection/f2e36a58802362203d214917413eacbec44cc25e6ecd3c5d7c4679d9f9d493fd" "q-97665/selection/ce8c2bcaef40d99863207e29506d40a17a312537ce24a742c9ed3d1ae307e6bf" "q-97665/selection/495e8813f59ee3e6319824a6a3a2161fda3a98a295c7e365f9389d8c70b6c8d4" "q-97665/selection/ec7ad9636cc54d887852e0674981ad4b02d15305f909ec6668bfa91951089a50" "q-97665/selection/beb61f7e98d5c8f83c610d16a577a27e9b26dd4a8e94eef9a7c5efedbe64b015"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97665" :question/id #uuid "c763e527-cc94-5b07-acc6-096b0d13fd01" :question/math-academy-id "q-97665" :question/problem "A particle $P$ moves along a counterclockwise circular path centered at $O$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity of $2\\,\\text{rad/s}.$ Given that the particle is located at $(7,0)$ when $t=0,$ find the velocity of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "The position function of a particle moving in a circular path of radius $R$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity $\\omega $ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t\\,j),\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that the circle is centered at $O,$ and the particle is at the position $(R,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nIn our case, we have $R=7$ and $\\omega =2\\text{ rad/s},$ so we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =7(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,j).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the velocity vector by differentiating the position vector. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =(7(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,j))^{′} \\\\  & =-14\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i+14\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the velocity vector at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =-14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,i+14\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,j \\\\  & =-14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\,i+14\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\,j \\\\  & =-\\frac{14\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,i+\\frac{14}{2}\\,j \\\\  & =-7\\sqrt{3}\\,i+7\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97665/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "77d9865d-2e8e-59fe-9a81-8935df037303"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97665"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97642/selection/8d5fd544bd3e578c00390e7c8f8335b40a4682c3eab40b8e0f96ff63a8e70725" :answer/id #uuid "f5c8d1a1-adac-57fe-b079-919db5d86869" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36\\text{ m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97642/selection/71180e9f13c33d25bb7d99af9ece6ca64f61dc990cfffc231f0354d740a74084" :answer/id #uuid "b630d3fb-e3fd-55f9-a1f3-99799896c03f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36\\pi \\text{ m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97642/selection/1bc1a9fbecc11d5e0e69d375508a66aa056c99734e79f13ac39b8fe9f2675186" :answer/id #uuid "73854352-7f76-5bcb-ade4-69448756ee88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\pi \\text{ m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97642/selection/b029bdd01e7339b7c414d4264c5593233225bd4c11ccc7d2bc573e2d447ed56c" :answer/id #uuid "7a384265-9622-5540-85c5-e910ae7e98e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\text{ m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97642/selection/1aaeff86cbb6b3f6eabea68978dfb4bcfe9d7711e4879ded3078ca8913c71dca" :answer/id #uuid "df1444a8-a824-59a1-8e9d-49e544441b64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\pi \\text{ m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97642/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e462ceb1-b01b-5c9a-baa3-aae3291ef579" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97642/selection/1aaeff86cbb6b3f6eabea68978dfb4bcfe9d7711e4879ded3078ca8913c71dca" :answer-field/choices ["q-97642/selection/8d5fd544bd3e578c00390e7c8f8335b40a4682c3eab40b8e0f96ff63a8e70725" "q-97642/selection/71180e9f13c33d25bb7d99af9ece6ca64f61dc990cfffc231f0354d740a74084" "q-97642/selection/1bc1a9fbecc11d5e0e69d375508a66aa056c99734e79f13ac39b8fe9f2675186" "q-97642/selection/b029bdd01e7339b7c414d4264c5593233225bd4c11ccc7d2bc573e2d447ed56c" "q-97642/selection/1aaeff86cbb6b3f6eabea68978dfb4bcfe9d7711e4879ded3078ca8913c71dca"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97642" :question/id #uuid "f49016e0-1c46-5368-90ce-8ec9a1e4ccdf" :question/math-academy-id "q-97642" :question/problem "An object moves along a circular path with position $r(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi t\\,j$ meters. Find the speed of the object at time $t,$ measured in seconds." :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we find the velocity vector by differentiating the position vector. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =(r(t))^{′} \\\\  & =(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi t\\,j)^{′} \\\\  & =-6\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi t\\,i+6\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed, we calculate the magnitude of the velocity vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}||v(t)|| & =\\sqrt{(-6\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi t)^{2}+(6\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36{\\pi }^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡2\\pi t+36{\\pi }^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡2\\pi t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36{\\pi }^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡2\\pi t+{cos}^{2}⁡2\\pi t)} \\\\  & =6\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed of the object is $6\\pi \\text{ m/s}.$\n\nNote that the speed is constant, but the velocity is not. \n\n**Method 2**\n\nFor uniform circular motion in the $xy$-plane, we have\n\n$$\n||v||=R|\\omega |,\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the radius of the circle, and $\\omega $ is the angular velocity.\n\nIn our case, the radius of the circle is $R=3\\,\\text{m}$ and the angular frequency $\\omega =2\\pi \\,\\text{rad/s}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n||v||=3\\cdot |2\\pi |=6\\pi \\text{ m/s}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-97642/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "77d9865d-2e8e-59fe-9a81-8935df037303"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97642"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97673/selection/4ae772f155f1f14a874cc56bbb90b4d94b18c4c97eb6a4a9c1df6ebf816d255a" :answer/id #uuid "fddff4e5-c024-57f7-88bb-7e5ecc5dbf8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-80\\,i+80\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97673/selection/e6a8bb590c81f4411e8bf4b1d5e456dc483d73945d519f8aac6402c96f6abd0a" :answer/id #uuid "c1ab8949-85aa-53c3-a291-0b861634e2c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-40\\,i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97673/selection/3c65d1b84eceb64f9bf9d454dc143aa3d8be36214bb101fc758c2a55e0f44ce6" :answer/id #uuid "2a5437e7-cec7-5baa-b191-606e7ca9f4f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-40\\,i-40\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97673/selection/2cc88a0aef987256cb1d086c3448d332af623cf9b0265521a64ae59810d2b4f1" :answer/id #uuid "78b47605-0617-58bc-88fc-dca88